\section{What the wide tables cannot express}{

A wide table has no place for the group designator, so attributes that
must be read as a group (a \verb{collision energy} and its \code{unit}, or the
members of a \verb{[n]MS:1003254|peak attribute} definition) arrive as
ordinary columns. Repeatable attributes are joined with \code{collapse}. Both
are visible again in \code{\link[=spectraCv]{spectraCv()}}, and \code{\link[=cvLosses]{cvLosses()}} reports how often
either occurs in a library - use it before trusting a wide table to be a
complete picture.
